This Power BI project showcases end-to-end dashboard creation from data cleaning to insightful visualization. The report is designed to extract actionable insights and support data-driven decision-making across key business metrics.

🧠 Project Goal

To build an interactive Power BI dashboard that demonstrates:
Data preparation and transformation
DAX-based KPI calculations
Visual storytelling using charts and slicers
Business insights through trend and category analysis

🧹 Data Preparation

Imported raw data from Excel/CSV (assumed)
Cleaned data using Power Query (null handling, type casting, column renaming)
Transformed categorical fields and date formats for consistency

🧮 DAX Measures & KPIs

Total Sales
Average Sales per Category/Segment
Customer Rating (if applicable)
Sales Trend Over Time
Product/Region Performance

📈 Visualizations

KPI Cards – Show top-level performance indicators
Bar/Column Charts – Sales by Category, Region, or Outlet
Line Charts – Monthly/Quarterly sales trends
Pie/Donut Charts – Proportional breakdowns by type
Slicers – Interactive filters for time, product, outlet, or geography
Tables – Drill-down views for deeper insights

🛠 Tools Used

Power BI Desktop (.pbix)
Power Query
DAX (Data Analysis Expressions)
Data modeling with star schema (assumed structure)

📂 How to Use

Open the BI Assignment.pbix file in Power BI Desktop
Review the data model, transformations, and DAX measures
Explore the dashboard with slicers and visualizations
Extend it by adding new metrics or connecting to live data

✅ Highlights

Clean and professional report layout
Modular design: easily scalable for new metrics
Reusable DAX logic and dynamic visuals
Clear storytelling with business relevance
